# Mechanism: wgpu-rendering

command: python3 -B scripts/check-wgpu-rendering.py
inputs:
  - .cairn/mechanisms
  - Cargo.toml
  - Cargo.lock
  - build.rs
  - src
  - crates
  - reactive-tui-macros
  - examples
  - tests
  - scripts
requirements:
  - GPU-002

The check must first prove its validator rejects a placeholder renderer, a
window or surface presentation path, missing texture readback, fixed terminal
dimensions, and absent cell-aspect correction. Corrected fixtures pass.

A feature-gated test renders the cube on a real, non-CPU adapter, records its
identity, requires nonuniform shaded pixels, and converts the result into the
existing Element/frame pipeline at 60x24, 144x50, and 200x60. A software
adapter or static CPU fixture cannot satisfy this requirement.
